# Project Tasks: Cross-Stitch Pattern Studio

## Phase 1: Foundation
- [x] 001: Initialize Vite project with React and TypeScript.
- [x] 002: Install core dependencies (Tailwind, Lucide, Zustand).
- [x] 003: Setup basic layout (Canvas area, Left Toolbar, Right Sidebar).
- [x] 004: Import DMC color database as a JSON utility.

## Phase 2: Core Grid Editor
- [x] 005: Build a high-performance `PixelGrid` component using HTML5 Canvas or SVG.
- [x] 006: Implement panning and zooming for the grid.
- [x] 007: Build the `DrawingTools` logic (Color selection, click-to-fill).
- [x] 008: Implement "Symbol View" toggle.

## Phase 3: Image-to-Chart Engine
- [x] 009: Create `ImageUploader` component.
- [x] 010: Implement image resizing and pixelation logic.
- [x] 011: Build color mapping utility (matching RGB to nearest DMC).
- [x] 012: Add "Palette Simplification" (limiting pattern to X colors).

## Phase 4: Export and Legends
- [x] 013: Build `PDFGenerator` utility.
- [x] 014: Design the printed legend template (Symbol | DMC Code | Name).
- [x] 015: Add thread length calculation logic.
- [x] 016: Add Export button to Header/Sidebar UI.
- [x] 017: Wire up PDF generation with project state (grid, palette, usage).
- [x] 018: Add download functionality for Pattern PDF and Shopping List.

## Phase 5: Advanced Features
- [x] 019: Implement 3D visualization on fabric textures.
- [x] 020: Add Quaker Ball geometric panel support (pentagon masking, assembly view).
- [x] 021: Implement project save/load (JSON export).
- [x] 022: Add material inventory tracking (skein management, usage alerts).

